<title>USA: Dell increases stock repurchase program.</title>
<headline>Dell increases stock repurchase program.</headline>
<dateline>ROUND ROCK, Texas 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dell Computer Corp said Thursday it authorized an 18 million share increase in its stock repurchase program, from 32 million shares to 50 million shares.</p>
<p>The amount of shares to be purchased and the timing of purchases of shares will be based on a number of factors, including the price of Dell's stock, the level of stock issuances under the employee stock plans and market conditions, the company said.</p>
<p>To date the company said it has repurchased about 21 million shares under the program and has secured options to purchase an additional 10 million shares with exercise dates through September 1997.</p>
</text>
